\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Chile central holds key rate steady, eyes strong peso\b0\par\par\uc2 1,015 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2013\par 17:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says peso has further appreciated in multilateral terms\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gov't met earlier Thursday to discuss peso strength\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at same level that triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011\par \par \uc2 (Recasts throughout; adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments, analyst quote)\par \par \uc2 By Anthony Esposito\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 11 (Reuters) - \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key rate steady at 5.0 percent on Thursday, as expected, and underscored that the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued appreciating across the board and that domestic demand remains dynamic.\par \par \uc2 It is the second meeting in a row the bank has referred to the peso's appreciation in "multilateral" terms in its post-meeting communique.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also mentioned that commodities prices, especially for copper - Chile's top export - have receded in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mentioned copper prices are falling yet the peso keeps appreciating reflects that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  notices an uncoupling of the peso with its fundamentals," said Alejandro Puente, economist at \uc2 BBVA Chile\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso typically moves in line with copper prices, as higher prices mean more dollars entering the local market due to sales of the red metal. The inverse is true of lower prices.\par \par \uc2 In a public display of unease with the matter, Finance Minister Felipe Larrain met with \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Rodrigo Vergara prior to the monetary policy meeting to discuss the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed to 465.50 per U.S. dollar on Tuesday - the same level that had triggered a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early 2011.\par \par \uc2 "We have a prior meeting with the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where we will discuss in depth the issue of the peso and other matters," Larrain told reporters earlier on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept its benchmark lending rate\par \par \uc2 steady at 5.0 percent since a surprise cut in January 2012, as buoyant growth, low inflation and a strong peso - as well as persistent economic threats from abroad - keep its hands tied.\par \par \uc2 "The labor market is still tight and domestic demand remains dynamic. Credit conditions are somewhat more restrictive," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its post-meeting statement.\par \par \uc2 Analysts surveyed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest poll said they saw the benchmark rate holding steady at least through December before being hiked to 5.25 percent within 11 months.\par \par \uc2 The bank kept its monetary policy bias broadly neutral, which in standard monetary policy parlance means it neither spurs nor curbs economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The peso has been buoyed by Chile's robust economy, an attractive rate differential and healthy prices for copper. So-called quantitative easing measures adopted in major economies have also helped fuel the peso's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The peso was one of the strongest performers against the U.S. dollar among 152 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters after appreciating 8.48 percent last year and has accumulated an additional gain of around 2 percent in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Though the peso "is likely to remain under strengthening pressure from capital inflows charged by global liquidity and attracted by solid fundamentals and high interest rates," there is limited room for additional appreciation, as an exchange rate closer to 460 per dollar increases the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said RBS economist Felipe Hernandez.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deployed a dollar-purchasing program in 2011, increasing its foreign reserves by $12 billion, to curb peso strength after it appreciated to 465.50 per dollar, then its highest level in over 2-1/2 years.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, the bank has said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the tools at its disposal, but it has also highlighted the costs associated with such a move.\par \par \uc2 SURGING DEMAND\par \par \uc2 The bank is also concerned with reining in robust domestic demand, which has been growing faster than gross domestic product, helping to fuel a widening current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have said the bank could raise its key rate to rein in buoyant demand sooner than forecast, but it may have to incur a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a rate hike to avoid further stoking the strong peso.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, bank board member Enrique Marshall said the bank will act if the local economy maintains dynamism "above what is reasonable," and interest rates are the best instrument at the entity's disposal.\par \par \uc2 Sturdy domestic demand, an economy near full employment and solid levels of investment have protected the world's No. 1 copper producer from a sharp slowdown on the back of global economic woes, but many analysts are now worried about overheating.\par \par \uc2 Those fears have not yet materialized in the form of inflationary pressures. Chile's consumer price index posted a 0.4 percent rise in March, its fastest pace since October, but the 12-month figure of 1.5 percent remained well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tolerance range of 2 percent to 4 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Headline and core inflation measures are around 1 percent and 2 percent year-on-year, while inflationary expectations in the policy horizon remain around the target," the post-meeting statement said.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the region, inflation in Brazil pierced the government's target ceiling in March for the first time in over a year. However, the rise was slightly less than expected, fueling bets the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could wait until May to start hiking interest rates.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, the annual inflation rate also climbed above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target ceiling in March, crimping policymakers' ability to lower borrowing costs as the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared to 20-month highs.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key rate to an all-time low of 4 percent in early March in what was seen as a bid to tamp down its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the peso has kept appreciating, and is up about 6.8 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Anthony Esposito, additional reporting by Santiago Newsoom and Moises Avila; editing by Bernadette Baum, G Crosse)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-CENBANK/RATES (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | NAT | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130411e94b000w1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\