\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Weaker After Finance Minister's 'Verbal  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 '\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sebastian Perez-Ferreiro   \par \uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2013\par 19:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The Chilean peso pulled back Wednesday from a 20-month high after what has been characterized as a "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " from \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister, who announced he would meet this week with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials to talk about the "worrisome" exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP468.50 to the dollar, down from Tuesday's close of CLP466.80, after trading in a range of CLP467.00 to CLP469.30.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit 20-month highs this week and seemed headed to the CLP465 level where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011, when it launched a $12 billion, year-long \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 Early Wednesday, though, the peso began to retreat as investors started closing out short positions and locking in profits, according to local traders. Then Finance Minister Felipe Larrain stepped in with what was widely seen as a "verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 "We are in full coordination mode with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We will meet either tomorrow or the following day [Thursday or Friday] with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president [Rodrigo Vergara]...without a doubt this is a situation that worries us," said the official, who sits on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly monetary policy meetings but doesn't vote on decisions, to reporters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its monetary policy meeting Thursday and may refer to the exchange rate in its policy statement issued immediately afterward.\par \par \uc2 "The peso was already retreating from its high against the dollar, add to it that Larrain will meet with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and all of that motivates people to close out short positions or bet on a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sending the peso lower," said Eugenio Cortes, a trader at EuroAmerica, who doesn't foresee an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the peso breaks through the CLP465 resistance level.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs closed at 2.59%, up from 2.57% Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs also closed higher, at 2.47%, from 2.46% the previous session. Bond yields move inversely to prices.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Sebastian Perez-Ferreiro at sebastian.perez-ferreiros@dowjones.com [ 10-04-13 1712GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130410e94a000sk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
