\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso ends near 2011  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  levels\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2013\par 19:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (New throughout, adds trader's comments, background details)\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, April 8 (Reuters) - Chile's peso ended at more than a year-and-a-half high on Monday, nearing levels that prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to launch a dollar-purchasing program in early 2011 to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2  The peso, which firmed 0.41 percent on Monday to bid at 466.90 per dollar, is up 2.53 percent so far in 2013.\par \par \uc2  The peso, which has been buoyed by Chile's robust economy, an attractive rate differential and healthy prices for top export copper, was one of the strongest performers against the U.S. dollar among 152 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters after appreciating 8.48 percent last year.\par \par \uc2  Exporters, especially fruit producers, in trade-intensive Chile have been walloped by the peso's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deployed a dollar-purchasing program in 2011, increasing its foreign reserves by $12 billion, to curb peso strength after it appreciated to its highest level in more than 2-1/2 years at 465.50 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  "Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested that it was comfortable with the real exchange rate's current levels, which triggered a supply (of dollars being sold) at the local level, especially by foreign brokerages. In other words they are doing carry-trade," a trader told Reuters.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last week the peso's real exchange rate had appreciated slightly and was on the low end of levels consistent with its long-term fundamentals.  The real exchange rate is a measure used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in part to gauge the competitiveness of Chilean exports.\par \par \uc2  Bank President Rodrigo Vergara said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one of the tools at the bank's disposal, but highlighted the costs associated with using that measure.\par \par \uc2  Analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could raise its key interest rate to rein in buoyant domestic demand sooner than forecast, but it may have to preface the hike with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid further strengthening the peso. \par \par \uc2  Over the weekend, bank board member Enrique Marshall said the bank will act if the local economy maintains dynamism "above what is reasonable," and interest rates are the best instrument at the entity's disposal. \par \par \uc2  Ebullient domestic demand, an economy nearing full employment and heavy investment have protected the world No.1 copper producer from a sharp slowdown on the back of global woes, but many analysts are now worried about overheating. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Froilan Romero and Moises Avila; Writing by Anthony Esposito; Editing by Leslie Adler and Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130408e948000ym\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
