\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Closes at 20-Month High, Near  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Levels\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sebastian Perez-Ferreiro   \par \uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2013\par 19:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The Chilean peso closed at a new 20-month high against the dollar Monday, extending the previous session's move toward levels at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP466.80 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP468.80, after trading in a range of CLP466.80 to CLP469.50.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke through the CLP470 resistance level of the past 18 months.\par \par \uc2 "The peso had a hard time breaking through the resistance level, but now we are clearly reaching probable \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, or at least that's how the market is viewing it," said Eugenio Cortes, a trader at EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 When the peso firmed to CLP465 in early 2011, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a $12 billion, year-long \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mario Del Campo, a trader at Banco Consorcio, believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in if the peso strengthens to a level around CLP460, "but only if there's a lot of pressure on the government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and right now I don't see the government too concerned about it."\par \par \uc2 The bank's latest monetary-policy report, released last week, showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees the peso trading in line with its fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged and weaker.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.53%, flat with Friday, and the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.45%, down from 2.49% the previous session. Bond yields move inversely to prices.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Sebastian Perez-Ferreiro at sebastian.perez-ferreiros@dowjones.com. [ 08-04-13 1730GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130408e948000qd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
