\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends At 20-Month High, Nearing  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Levels\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sebastian Perez-Ferreiro   \par \uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2013\par 19:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The Chilean peso closed at a 20-month high against the dollar, breaking through a significant resistance level and nearing levels at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP468.80 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP470.00, after trading in a range of CLP468.60 to CLP471.30.\par \par \uc2 "According to fundamentals, the peso should have weakened today, but there's likely a big dollar sale in the market underpinning the peso," said Gloria Soto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at FXCM Chile.\par \par \uc2 When the peso firmed to CLP465 in early 2011, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a $12 billion, year-long \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "At these levels, we expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will start buying dollars soon," Ms. Soto said.\par \par \uc2 But not all market participants agree, as some see the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk closer to CLP460.\par \par \uc2 In the last two sessions, large dollar sales from institutional investors have given the peso strength.\par \par \uc2 "On Thursday, it was mining companies. Today, it was the private pension-fund managers," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Flavio Magnasco.\par \par \uc2 "Only the dollar sales flows have taken the peso below CLP470, because all the other signs point to a weakening exchange rate for the peso."\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower in reaction to a lower-than-expected gain in a gross domestic proxy index for February.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported the Imacec GDP proxy index grew 3.8% year-on-year in February, well below the 5.1% analysts expected.\par \par \uc2 A deceleration in economic activity pushes a possible rate increase further away.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs closed at 2.53%, down from 2.56% Thursday, and the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.49%, down from 2.56% the previous session. Bond yields move inversely to prices.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Sebastian Perez-Ferreiro at sebastian.perez-ferreiros@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This item was corrected at 1:51 p.m. EDT to show that Gloria Soto in the third paragraph the peso should have weakened. The original incorrectly stated the peso should have firmed. [ 05-04-13 1731GMT ]\par \par \uc2 ("\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends at 20-Month High, Nearing \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Levels," at 1:31 p.m. EDT, misquoted Gloria Soto in the third paragraph as saying the peso should have firmed. She said the peso should have weakened. [ 05-04-13 1750GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130405e945000oc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
