\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Closes Weaker on Chinese, U.S. Manufacturing Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2013\par 18:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso closed weaker against the dollar Monday on disappointing Chinese and U.S. manufacturing data.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at CLP472.30 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP471.50, after trading in a range between CLP472.10 and CLP473.20.\par \par \uc2 As China and the U.S. are among Chile's main trading partners, the peso often takes its cues from U.S. and Chinese economic developments.\par \par \uc2 The peso has been trading between CLP470 and CLP475 to the dollar since the beginning of the year and traders are looking for volatility.\par \par \uc2 "It's boring," said Martin Ferrer, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk at Capital \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic growth and speculation about a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the peso cross the CLP470 resistance level have kept the Andean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading rangebound, Mr. Ferrer added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the peso firmed to the CLP465 level to the dollar in early January 2011. It bought a total $12 billion at a rate of $50 million a day during that year.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged from Thursday in a quiet session.\par \par \uc2 The yields on five-year BCUs closed at 2.60% and the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.54%. Bond yields and prices move inversely.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This item was corrected at 1:26 p.m. ET to fix the misspelled last name of the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk at Capital \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fifth and sixth paragraphs. His last name is Ferrer, not Fierro. [ 01-04-13 1656GMT ]\par \par \uc2 "Chile Peso Closes Weaker on Chinese, U.S. Manufacturing Data," at 1656 GMT, misspelled the last name of the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk at Capital \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fifth and sixth paragraphs. His last name is Ferrer, not Fierro. [ 01-04-13 1725GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130401e941000d3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
