\par\par \b \uc2 Finance Minister Says Chile Studying Measures to Weaken Peso - Newspaper\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2013\par 18:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Chilean government is studying measures to weaken the peso, such as limiting state companies' dollar-denominated debt, La Tercera newspaper reported Sunday, citing Finance Minister Felipe Larrain.\par \par \uc2 The peso's appreciation versus the U.S. dollar has prompted agricultural, wine and manufactured-goods exporters' calls to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government to weaken the peso as a strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurts exports' competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Like other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, the peso has strengthened around 10% to the dollar since early 2012, but unlike the authorities of Colombia, Peru or Brazil, the \uc2 Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has chosen not to act over the past year.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  depends solely on the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision.\par \par \uc2 "Should the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we would support it," Mr. Larrain said to La Tercera.\par \par \uc2 Among the steps to limit dollar inflows to Chile, the government could reduce state companies' bond issues abroad. Copper producer \uc2 Corporacion Nacional del Cobre de Chile\uc2 , or Codelco, and oil and gas company \uc2 Empresa Nacional del Petroleo SA\uc2 , or Enap, are some of the state-owned firms that issued debt in dollars in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The Finance Minister also ruled out establishing controls on foreign capital, arguing they don't limit the total amount of dollars arriving in Chile and make credit more expensive.\par \par \uc2 The government recently announced a local debt program of as much as $5 billion for 2013. In 2012, it had a program for as much as $6 billion.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-24-13 1238ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020130224e92o00013\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
