\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \uc2 Chile  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Holds at 5%, Bias Still Neutral\b0\par\par\uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2013\par 23:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighs robust local economy against a still risky international outlook\par \par \uc2 --Base rate seen at 5% at least through the first half\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in peso market just yet, analysts say\par \par \uc2 (Updates with comments from analysts starting in paragraph fourteen)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Carolina Pica \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SANTIAGO, Chile--For the 12th consecutive month, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Chile\f28 \uc2 \f2  kept its benchmark interest rate steady, while maintaining its neutral rate bias.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At its monthly monetary-policy meeting Thursday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held the overnight interbank lending rate, known locally as the TPM, at 5%, in line with analysts' expectations. The 13 economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires had expected the bank to stand at 5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Like it did in its previous 11 meetings, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weighed contrasting factors such as the risks stemming from the euro zone and the U.S. and the performance of the local economy, which has grown at a robust pace with mild inflation and low unemployment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In January-November 2012, the country's gross domestic proxy index grew 5.7%, surpassing expectations that GDP grew 5.5% in the whole of 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation, according to recently reported data, ended 2012 at 1.5%, below the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target of 3%, with a tolerance range of one percentage point around that target.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In its post-meeting communique, the bank said activity and demand are in line with its outlook and, while inflation is below 2%, long-term inflation expectations are in line with its target.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also briefly mentioned the peso's strength versus the dollar. A wide spread with U.S. rates, relatively high copper prices, the dollar's global weakness and the resilience of the local economy have all contributed to firming the Andean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In this recent month, the peso has appreciated slightly with respect to the dollar," it said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In recent sessions, the peso has been trading near a psychologically important level at CLP470 and flirting with the CLP465 trading level that triggered the bank's $12 billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program in early 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the international front, the bank said that while there are still risks in the euro zone and the U.S., international financial conditions have improved.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the economies of developed nations remain weak while China, Chile's main trade partner, is showing positive signs of growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The prices of fuels abroad have increased, while copper, the country's biggest export, has held at prices similar to those seen in December, the bank said. International crude oil prices can pressure local inflation as the country imports 98% of the fuels it consumes. A strong peso, however, relieves some of these pressures as imports get cheaper when the peso firms.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank maintained its neutral rate bias, reiterating, as in previous months, that any future changes to the TPM will depend on the impact of domestic and international macroeconomic conditions on inflation expectations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts, meanwhile, don't foresee any changes in monetary policy for most of 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For the bank to make any move, the outlook abroad would have to improve dramatically while the economy here decelerates and inflation moves closer to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target," said Cristobal Doberti, chief economist at local investment bank BICE Inversiones.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts expect the TPM to hold steady at 5% at least through the first half of the year. The bank's most recent monthly poll of analysts' expectations shows a rate increase isn't expected until sometime in the second half of this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "When the international outlook takes a turn for the better, we could see a rate increase," said Felip Jaque, senior economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (BBVACL.SN) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unit .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Regarding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said the bank's mention of the slight firming the peso has seen in recent sessions is a signal that it won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unless the peso strengthens further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most analysts think the peso will have to cross the CLP460-threshold before the bank begins buying dollars to weaken the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Despite the small change in language from last month's statement, the bank is saying that at these levels, it won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Mr. Doberti said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In recent public appearances, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Rodrigo Vergara has said that while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't be ruled out, it's a costly measure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Graciela Ibanez contributed to this article\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Carolina Pica at carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 17-01-13 2217GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130117e91h000wl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
