\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Unchanged Amid More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Calls\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2013\par 18:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso closed flat against the dollar Thursday remaining at a three-month high as large local institutional investors bought the greenback offsetting dollar sales from local banks.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP470.70 to the dollar, same as on Wednesday, after trading in a narrow range of CLP470.20 to CLP471.50.\par \par \uc2 Chile's private pension-fund managers, or AFPs, and local companies bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while local banks sold their dollar positions, said Eugenio Cortes, a trader at EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 After exporters of manufactured goods asked for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, agricultural exporters made a similar call Thursday as a strong peso is hurting their competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Traders see the dollar at CLP470 in coming days, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most recent poll of financial-market traders.\par \par \uc2 "We think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso crosses CLP470 [to the dollar]," said Mr. Cortes.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a yearlong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program when the peso firmed to the CLP465 level versus the greenback in early 2011.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in a quiet session.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs ended at 2.72%, down from 2.80% on Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.72%, same as on the previous session. Bond yields and bond prices move inversely.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 10-01-13 1716GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130110e91a0012g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
