\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Chile Peso Strengthens Tracking US Stock Futures\b0\par\par\uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2012\par 13:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 7:11 EST - Chilean peso slightly higher versus the dollar as U.S. stock futures rise on hopes budget talks in that country will continue to progress. \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't mention \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its latest Monetary Policy Report, released Tuesday. With a few days left to end the year, it isn't likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 2012. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a yearlong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program when the peso firmed to CLP465.40 against the greenback in early 2011. Dollar recently trading at CLP473.90 versus Tuesday's close of CLP474.20, according to Valor Futuro newswire. (graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:07 EST - Roughly 2% volume growth at \uc2 General Mills\uc2  (GIS) excluding acquisitions and contained cost increases help the packaged-foods giant easily beat consensus F2Q EPS estimates and prompts GIS to say profit for the year could top its prior forecast. However, the high end of GIS' latest target is merely the mean estimate of Wall Street's current range of forecasts, so there's nothing terribly unexpected on that front. But in light of the 2Q profit, analysts are liable to boost their view beyond what GIS is now anticipating. Investors were expecting some good news as shares had risen steadily the past 5 weeks, climbing nearly 7% in closing at an all-time high Tuesday. GIS is inactive premarket. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:52 EST - Some have bouquets ready amid the F2Q rebound \uc2 Oracle\uc2  (ORCL) saw in Europe. Constant-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenue from the company's license and cloud-subscription business in Europe, the Middle East and Africa jumped 12% last quarter, notes Janney, after rising by a low-single-digit rate the prior 6. "Our checks indicate that its business in Europe is in the upswing ,driven by healthy activity around large deals and improving sales productivity," the investment bank adds. It things the momentum there will persist "well into next FY." Mizuho calls ORCL's performance in that region "clearly impressive in the current macro backdrop." It adds ORCL's report bodes well for fellow software company Red Hat (RHT), which releases F3Q results Thursday. ORCL is up 2.1% premarket while RHT is inactive. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:42 EST - The real is up sharply against the dollar as \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out an auction of dollar credit lines for a 3rd-consecutive day. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises to BRL2.0776/dollar from Tuesday's close of BRL2.0879 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells up to $2B via dollar credit lines with a commitment to repurchase on Feb. 1. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has worked feverishly this week to counter heavy year-end dollar outflows that have caused the real to weaken anew. Brazil is keen to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contained to its recent trading range of BRL2-2.10. (jeff.fick@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 6:32 EST - With Harman's (HAR) speaker business having stabilized amid the company's big move into emerging markets the past several years, the high-end product maker is making what seems to be a logical extension effort--going into professional lighting. It's agreed to pay EUR110M ($146M) for Denmark's Martin, which provides concert and other entertainment lighting that can be paired with HAR's audio offerings. Holding company Schouw (SCHO.KO) owns Martin, which has revenue last year of EUR150M. The deal has given shares of SCHO.KO, already up strongly this year, a further lift, rising 6.3% in hitting an 18-month high after trading sideways since early August. HAR, inactive premarket, has jumped some 18% the past month after swooning 1/4 the prior 2.\par \par \uc2 6:19 EST - US stock-index futures continue to march ahead after a 2nd-straight day of stout advances. The fuzzy feelings--be it from the fiscal cliff or the coming holidays--continue to have bulls buoyant and bears sleepy. That is liable to continue in the very short-term as volume continues to dry up into year-end, unless--of course--there some fresh headline that puts the kibosh on all the current euphoria. Who knows, it might even come from \uc2 FedEx\uc2 's (FDX) F2Q report next hour. Also on tap this morning is November housing starts. Dow-industrial futures are up 37 points and the S&P 500 rises 3. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Shipman\f28 \uc2 \f2 , 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 12-19-12 0712ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020121219e8cj0004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
