\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Weaker; Traders Focus on U.S. Budget Talks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2012\par 18:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso closed slightly weaker against the dollar Wednesday in a quiet session as investors continued to focus on U.S. budget negotiations, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market hasn't been needed this year.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP474.50 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP474.20, after trading in a range of CLP473.80 to CLP475.40.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is an export-based economy, the peso often takes its cues from U.S. economic developments as they signal the direction of global growth.\par \par \uc2 The peso has strengthened about 8% against the dollar so far this year, prompting exporters to ask the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the peso. \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, didn't mention \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its latest Monetary Policy Report, released Tuesday, and on Wednesday Gov. Rodrigo Vergara reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has its costs. A strong peso makes \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports less competitive.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso doesn't cross the CLP465 level versus the dollar," said Francisco Schneider, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Celfin Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a yearlong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program when the peso firmed to CLP465.40 versus the dollar in early 2011.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in a quiet session as the end of the year approaches.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs ended at 2.57%, up from 2.55% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.49%. Bond yields and prices move inversely.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 19-12-12 1716GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121219e8cj000t9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
