\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Hasn't Been Needed - \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Head\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2012\par 16:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been warranted as peso still in line with fundamentals\par \par \uc2 --Growth seen robust in 2013, but economy faces domestic and external risks\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerned about possible housing bubble; Government rules out bubble forming\par \par \uc2 (Updates with more comments from Rodrigo Vergara and Finance Minister Felipe Larrain)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the peso market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar as this "hasn't been necessary," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rodrigo Vergara said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 As the peso has firmed some 8% versus the dollar this year, exporters have clamored for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or government moves to depreciate the peso. Exports, the backbone of the Chilean economy, lose competitiveness when the peso firms.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vergara, speaking at the Icare local business forum and later to reporters, reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be costly.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has its benefits and it has its costs and while it's a policy that's always available, we will use it if the benefits outweigh the costs," he said, adding that the peso remains in line with its long-term fundamentals although on the stronger end of the bank's tolerance levels.\par \par \uc2 In early 2011, when the peso was trading at near three-year highs, the bank launched a year-long, $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 "If we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in previous occasions, it was because we saw the benefits of such a move," the central banker said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released its quarterly Monetary Policy Report and its most recent Financial Stability Report.\par \par \uc2 In the former, it raised its outlook for both 2012 and 2013, while pointing out that the economy, which has been growing at a brisk pace, isn't immune to both internal and external risks.\par \par \uc2 The bank raised its 2012 gross domestic product outlook to a year-on-year gain of 5.5%, in line with analysts and markets.\par \par \uc2 "Growth this year has been surprisingly high," Mr. Vergara said, adding that the bank's initial growth view was a percentage point lower than its recently revised estimate.\par \par \uc2 GDP is expected to grow between 4.25% and 5.25% in 2013, on the bank of healthy domestic demand and investments, while facing risks from the slowdown in the euro zone and a widening current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also mentioned a possible housing bubble as a risk to the local economy. In its Financial Stability Report, the bank said strong real estate demand had boosted housing prices in certain areas to record highs, which could lead to a potential surge in medium-term mortgage lending.\par \par \uc2 "We didn't use the phrase 'housing bubble' as it can lead to misunderstandings, but there's been a steep price increase along with significant debt which can produce a vulnerability. So our first move is to issue a warning about what could happen in the future," Mr. Vergara said.\par \par \uc2 Finance Miniter Felipe Larrain, meanwhile, applauded the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's revised outlook as it is in line with the government's view but ruled out a nascent housing bubble.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Larrain told reporters the government is monitoring the real estate sector to avert any such bubble.\par \par \uc2 Write to Carolina Pica at carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 19-12-12 1554GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121219e8cj000ra\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
