\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Marginally Higher; Peso Closed Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2012\par 21:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Chile's IPSA select-stock index closed marginally higher in a quiet session Wednesday as the end of the year approaches and traders refrain from placing bold bets.\par \par \uc2 The IPSA ended 0.06% higher, at 4291.08, while trading volume declined to 98.80 billion Chilean pesos ($208.2 million) from CLP111.76 billion Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Energy holding company \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) ended 0.07% lower at CLP174.38 ahead of Thursday's shareholders meeting to vote on a disputed $5.96 billion capital increase, which would be the largest locally on record.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Enersis\uc2  deal is likely to be approved, said Rodrigo Arriagada, an analyst at Alikanto Servicios Financieros.\par \par \uc2 The energy company's controlling shareholder, Spanish company \uc2 Endesa SA\uc2  (ELEZY, ELE.MC), has said it will offer 16.44 billion shares at CLP173 each. \uc2 Endesa\uc2  would subscribe to the increase with $3.62 billion in non-cash assets, such as stakes in Latin American utilities, while minority shareholders would subscribe with $2.34 billion in cash.\par \par \uc2 Private-pension fund manager \uc2 AFP Provida\uc2  (PVD, PROVIDA.SN), meanwhile, closed 0.3% higher at CLP3,248.10. Press reports on Wednesday stated U.S. life insurer \uc2 MetLife\uc2  (MET) is in talks to buy \uc2 Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria\uc2 's (\uc2 BBVA\uc2 , BBVA.MC) 51.6% stake in Provida in a deal valued at about $2 billion.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso closed slightly weaker against the dollar in a quiet session as investors continued to focus on U.S. budget negotiations, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market hasn't been needed this year.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP474.50 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP474.20, after trading in a range of CLP473.80 to CLP475.40.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is an export-based economy, the peso often takes its cues from U.S. economic developments as they signal the direction of global growth.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in a quiet session as the end of the year approaches.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs ended at 2.57%, up from 2.55% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.49%. Bond yields and prices move inversely.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 19-12-12 2032GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121219e8cj000v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
