\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: \uc2 UBS\uc2  Cuts \uc2 Apple\uc2  Estimates on iPhone Questions\b0\par\par\uc2 971 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2012\par 14:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 8:31 EST - \uc2 UBS\uc2  cuts its estimates for \uc2 Apple\uc2 's (AAPL) 2013 earnings to levels below Wall Street consensus, and reduces its target price 10%, to $700 from $780. While Analyst Steven Milunovich keeps his buy rating, he cites signs the iPhone's rate of production is falling. He says some of his contacts in China think the iPhone 5 might not do as well as the 4S there, and adds that the iPad mini might be "cannibalizing" larger iPad sales. "The stock has been a tug of war between low valuation and peaking growth and margins." AAPL down 1.8% at $520 premarket. (alexandra.scaggs@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:24 EST - A consumer-price inflation reading just ahead, but this report will likely only have a brief impact on Treasurys, if any. The Fed has said its part, committing to further stimulus, and a weak reading only affirms the move, while an uptick in prices will likely be brushed off as temporary. Treasury investors' focus is squarely on the fiscal cliff now, as a budget deal (or the lack of one) will set the outlook for 2013 growth. Ten-year notes flat to yield 1.727%. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:22 EST - \uc2 Apple\uc2  (AAPL) is shedding 1.9% in the premarket to $519.22, which puts the stock on track to open just above last week's low of $518.63, after the former Teflon tech giant was found to have infringed on some mobile-device patents. There has been some early indication that AAPL might be starting to build a platform for a short-term bottom. Despite declining four of the last five days, yesterday's low stayed above Monday's low, which was above last week's low. Lack of downside progress is the first sign that bulls are gaining the initiative. If AAPL falls below $518.63, the November low of $505.65 becomes the target. (tomi.kilgore@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:01 EST - Brazil's Eletropaulo is slumping more than 7% after courts decided that the company is solely responsible for repayment of a BRL1.3B loan. The loan was granted by federal utility holding Eletrobras before Eletropaulo was privatized, and the companies had been arguing over who was responsible for repayment. CTEEP, which took over some other Eletropaulo assets when it was privatized, wasn't found to be responsible for repayment. CTEEP shares are up 0.6% in Sao Paulo trading. (paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:50 EST - \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  downgrades \uc2 Exxon Mobil\uc2  (XOM) to neutral from buy, noting its "relative outperformance" of the Energy Select Sector ETF (XLE) this year "on its defensive characteristics which trumped disappointing E&P segment performance." Goldman says it's favoring less defensive energy stocks as the firm's economists predict a recovery in global GDP in 2013. "Our call for a secular upturn in the super majors CVX and XOM now appears to be deferred until 2014 given recent E&P segment disappointments at both companies," firm adds. XOM off 0.5% at $88.12 premarket. (john.shipman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:50 EST - Needham cuts its recommendation of \uc2 Endo Health Solutions\uc2  (ENDP) to under perform after yesterday's earnings warning, citing "continued deterioration in core franchises, execution missteps and underwhelming operating performance in acquired non-pharma segments." Firm does say a near-term stock bounce is possible due to current depressed levels, but worries about the implications of recent guidance reductions on company's prior 2013-2015 outlook. Needham doesn't see a change in leadership, after CEO \uc2 David Holveck\uc2  announced plan to retire next year, as being able to quickly fix structural risks. EDNP is inactive premarket and down 20% over the last three months. (patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:39 EST - Chilean peso rises to near a two-month high on China's upbeat manufacturing data. China is Chile's main trading partner and largest copper customer. \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, held the interest rate at 5% and, in its post-monetary policy meeting communique, mentioned the peso's appreciation against the dollar. "By saying that, the bank opened the door to a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sergio Tricio, an analyst at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank launched a year-long \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program when the peso firmed to 465.40 against the dollar in early 2011. Dollar recently trading at CLP474.00 versus Thursday's close of CLP474.70, according to Valor Futuro newswire. (graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:30 EST - Bulls angling for an early rebound after yesterday's selloff, though there's no clear catalyst emerging yet to drive positive sentiment. Strong gains in Shanghai overnight could be offering some support, with investors there hoping for more government action to spur stronger growth in China. European markets are mixed, offering little early leadership for US stocks. November CPI due at 8:30am ET, followed by industrial production & capacity utilization at 9:15am. S&P futures up 3.75; 10-yr note little changed, yield at 1.73%. (john.shipman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:19 EST - Brazil's economic growth is likely to remain volatile as the government opts for "microeconomic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " such as tax cuts on auto sales, rather than wider-reaching reform, Espirito Santo bank says. The government's stimulus measures have also focused on consumption, while investment withers, which will make difficult efforts to control inflation, BES says. (paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 12-14-12 0832ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020121214e8ce0004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
