\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  gain modestly after Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2012\par 21:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Fed pledges to pump more money into the U.S. economy\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso gains for 7th session to 2-month high\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real gains 0.1 pct, Mexico peso flat\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Dec 12 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose modestly on Wednesday after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  pledged to inject more money into the U.S. economy, potentially driving up dollar inflows to emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's decision to replace an expiring stimulus program with a fresh round of Treasury debt purchases, combined with its pledge to keep interest rates near zero until the jobless rate falls to 6.5 percent, is likely to keep alive investor appetite for emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks.\par \par \uc2 A number of domestic factors curbed gains in Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, however.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, a holiday kept local markets closed, leaving the peso to trade nearly unchanged at 12.740 per dollar in overseas trading.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , investors grew increasingly cautious of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the peso gained for a seventh consecutive session.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended 0.17 percent higher at 474.20 per dollar, its strongest level in two months, also helped by a rise in prices of copper, the country's main export product.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real ended 0.1 percent stronger at 2.0742 per dollar, also supported by two \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions of dollars with repurchase agreements.\par \par \uc2 The auctions are aimed at providing dollar liquidity at year-end, but also suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want the real to weaken too much for fear of inflation.\par \par \uc2 "The recent actions and comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials show the bank wants a stronger real as they fear inflation pressures," said Sidnei Nehme, a director at NGO brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2015 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            Daily  YTD pct\par                                      pct   change\par                          Latest   change  \par Brazil real                2.0742     0.13    -9.79\par                                           \par Mexico peso               12.7400    -0.03     9.65\par                                           \par Argentina peso*            6.4600    -0.31   -26.78\par                                           \par Chile peso               474.2000     0.17     9.51\par                                           \par Colombia peso          1,794.6500     0.33     8.01\par                                           \par Peru sol                   2.5650     0.23     5.15\par                                           \par * Argentine peso's rate between                    \par brokerages                                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Danielle Fonseca in Sao Paulo; Editing by Dan Grebler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | C | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121215e8cc0008j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\pics