\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm; Venezuela bonds rally\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2012\par 22:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Venezuelan 2027 bond hits highest price since January 2008\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso up again, some see cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso up 0.5 pct, Brazil real flat\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Dec 11 (Reuters) - Venezuelan bonds rallied for a second session on Tuesday on expectations of a regime change in the oil-exporting nation, while Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose as German data on investor confidence and hopes of a U.S. budget deal supported appetite for risk.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela's global 2027 bonds, the most actively traded, reached their highest price since early 2008 as President \uc2 Hugo Chavez\uc2  underwent surgery in Cuba for a cancer recurrence, raising the prospect of new presidential elections, even as Chavez named a successor.\par \par \uc2 The 2027 bonds last traded 1.4 points higher at a bid price of 102.367.\par \par \uc2 Yield spreads between Venezuelan bonds and safe-haven U.S. Treasuries tightened 3 basis points to 749 basis points according to \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's EMBI+ index, showing investors' appetite for the country's assets was the strongest since September 2008.\par \par \uc2 Before leaving Venezuela, Chavez named his vice president and foreign minister, Nicolas Maduro, to take over, should he become incapacitated. Chavez, who is due to begin a new six-year term on Jan. 10, urged supporters to vote for Maduro in the event of an election.\par \par \uc2 "We are encouraged that President Chavez asked for voter support for his candidate since this suggests an electoral transition as opposed to the alternative strategy to allow the VP to finish the entire six-year term," Siobhan Morden, head of Latin America strategy at \uc2 Jefferies & Co. Inc\uc2 ., wrote in a research note.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  GAIN, EXCEPT REAL\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Latin America, most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose after a key index of German investor sentiment rose sharply in December, supporting optimism about the world economy.\par \par \uc2 The appetite for risk further grew as the S&P 500 index\par \par \uc2 ended at its best level since Election Day, buoyed by hopes of a resolution to the U.S. budget impasse.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso rose 0.5 percent to 12.7435 per dollar, while the Chilean peso edged 0.1 percent higher to 475.00 per greenback, its strongest level in nearly two months.\par \par \uc2 It was the sixth straight winning session for the Chilean peso, which led some traders to believe the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon act to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the Brazilian real closed practically unchanged at 2.0770 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced two auctions on Wednesday to sell as much as $1.5 billion on the spot market with repurchase agreement.\par \par \uc2 The announcement added to the market perception that Brazilian policymakers do not want the real to weaken. Confirming that perception, a member of Brazil's economic team said the real was at a satisfactory level when it traded around 2.03 and 2.04 reais per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2121 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                          Latest           \par Brazil