\par\par \b \uc2 Chile CorpGroup Still Interested in Local Fuel Assets - Chairman\b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2012\par 13:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --CorpGroup would be interested in fuel company \uc2 Terpel\uc2 's local assets\par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Terpel\uc2  has 97 convenience stores in Chile, an attractive target for CorpGroup's retail division\par \par \uc2 --"We're interested in the real-estate and the convenience store businesses," CorpGroup Chairman says\par \par \uc2 By Graciela Ibanez\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Chile--After more than 70 acquisitions in the retail sector over the past five years, Chilean conglomerate CorpGroup SA still has an appetite for another deal and would again bid for fuel company \uc2 Terpel\uc2 's local assets should the opportunity arise, said CorpGroup Chairman Alvaro Saieh.\par \par \uc2 That opportunity may come soon enough, given a deadline for \uc2 Terpel\uc2 's controlling shareholder to sell the unit. If a renewed bid by CorpGroup is ultimately successful, it will consolidate CorpGroup as one of Chile's top convenience store operators, and would add significantly to its real-estate holdings.\par \par \uc2 "We're interested in the real-estate and the convenience-store businesses, but we would need a partner [to run \uc2 Terpel\uc2 's 200 gas stations]," Mr. Saieh said in an interview last month.\par \par \uc2 Terpel\uc2  has 97 convenience stores in Chile.\par \par \uc2 In 2011, Mr. Saieh's CorpGroup, along with state-owned oil company \uc2 Empresa Nacional del Petroleo SA\uc2 , or Enap, and Peruvian conglomerate Grupo Romero, bid for \uc2 Terpel\uc2 's Chilean assets, but lost to holding company \uc2 Quinenco SA\uc2  (QUINENCO.SN), which had offered $320 million to \uc2 Terpel\uc2 's controller, Chilean fuel and forestry conglomerate \uc2 Empresas Copec SA\uc2  (COPEC.SN).\par \par \uc2 Terpel\uc2  Chile could be up for sale again if the Supreme Court upholds an April Antitrust Court ruling that rejected Quinenco's bid, as the holding company already has a 13% market share in the fuel distribution sector. The Supreme Court doesn't have a date for its ruling.\par \par \uc2 Copec is under a separate antitrust deadline to divest its \uc2 Terpel\uc2  Chilean assets by the end of November.\par \par \uc2 Terpel\uc2 's convenience stores are an attractive target for CorpGroup's SMU retail division and real-estate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SMU, which plans to consolidate its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the next two years after a flurry of acquisitions in Chile and Peru, has developed the convenience store format in Chile's largest cities.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean retailer, which reported a 29% increase in sales to 1.029 trillion pesos ($2.16 billion) in the first-half of the year, plans to finance its organic growth by raising cash from listing shares on the Santiago Stock Exchange and in the U.S. next year.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Saieh said he won't venture SMU into a new country, such as Colombia, where CorpGroup has been aggressively expanding this year through its banking unit \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2  (BCA, CORPBANCA.SN).\par \par \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2 , Chile's fifth largest bank in terms of loans, will consolidate its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Colombia over the next two years after it purchased the Colombian unit of Spanish \uc2 Banco Santander SA\uc2  (SAN, SAN.MC) and closes the acquisition of Colombian \uc2 Helm Bank SA\uc2  (PFHELMBAN.BO) in the first quarter of 2013.\par \par \uc2 "The Colombian market offers big expansion opportunities as it's less developed than the Chilean market and Colombia has a population that is three times Chile's," Mr. Saieh said.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, Chilean banks are the most active lenders, with domestic credit to the private sector at some 70% of the country's gross domestic product. In Colombia it's about 45% of GDP, according to the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Colombia, \uc2 CorpBanca\uc2 , which will have a 7% market share after the \uc2 Helm Bank\uc2  acquisition, plans to target middle and lower income individuals as it already has a presence in the higher income segment, Mr. Saieh said on the 45-million people country.\par \par \uc2 As a long-time banker, Mr. Saieh jumped into \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  discussion after the peso has firmed nearly 8% versus the dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 "If \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was easy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have already done it."\par \par \uc2 With the peso at CLP482 to the dollar, agricultural exporters are asking the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the Andean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a strong peso hurts their revenue.\par \par \uc2 In 2011, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a yearlong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program when the peso firmed to CLP465.40 in early January of last year.\par \par \uc2 A similar move isn't likely at the moment as the peso is still in line with its fundamentals, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rodrigo Vergara has said several times.\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 11-14-12 0729ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020121114e8be0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
