\par\par \b \uc2 Chileans Debate a  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  as Peso Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2012\par 20:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The debate over whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should try to weaken the peso heated up this week as the peso remains strong against the dollar, but a consensus about such a measure is still far off.\par \par \uc2 With the peso closing Tuesday at CLP472.80 to the dollar, the Andean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has firmed 10% against the greenback this year, making it one of the world's top gainers versus the dollar in 2012.\par \par \uc2 The peso's current trading level is close to the CLP465 level seen in January 2011, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a yearlong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program and bought a total of $12 billion at a rate of $50 million a day.\par \par \uc2 While market participants say the current level is enough to justify an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they agree there's little the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do when the dollar weakens against most of the world's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The peso isn't as out of line with its fundamentals as it was in the past and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has more dollar reserves than in 2011," said Sergio Tricio, head of research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One of the reasons for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to accumulate reserves, former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Vittorio Corbo recently said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to 15% of gross domestic product with its 2011 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday, President Sebastian Pinera jumped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate and attributed the strong peso to the previous administration's increase in public spending.\par \par \uc2 "If we raise public spending, we will further strengthen the peso," Mr. Pinera said in a radio interview, after having recently sent to Congress the country's 2013 budget. That fiscal budget will grow 4.8% year-on-year to some $62 billion, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimates gross domestic product will grow between 4.75% and 5.25% this year.\par \par \uc2 "To control the peso/dollar parity, we're implementing responsible fiscal policy," Mr. Pinera said.\par \par \uc2 To calm agricultural producers' calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Pinera said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will take measures when it deems these are appropriate. Chile is an export-based economy and the country's revenue decreases when the peso strengthens.\par \par \uc2 For a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be effective in weakening the peso, the bank will have to buy a total of about $10 billion, analysts said. With the 2011 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its $12 billion purchase, the peso weakened some 8% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "If we want to reach a similar effect this year, the bank should buy $12 billion or more," said Nathan Pincheira, senior analyst at Banchile Inversiones.\par \par \uc2 Another factor to consider in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  scenario is the need to offset the economic effects of the increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. In 2011, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued $2 billion in short-term fixed-income instruments and $10 billion in both peso-denominated and inflation-indexed bonds to neutralize the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The 2011 sterilization plan triggered an increase of around 90 basis points in the yield of 10-year peso-denominated bonds and 30 basis points in the yield of 10-year inflation-indexed bonds," said Mr. Pincheira.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rodrigo Vergara, meanwhile, has reiterated that the costs of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would outweigh the benefits of such a move.\par \par \uc2 Despite the high costs, if the peso continues to strengthen against the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anyway as the government isn't likely to adjust fiscal policy to cool down the appreciating pressures on the peso, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 02-10-12 1821GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121002e8a2000ue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
