\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Central Banker: No Set Level for Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 - Newspaper\b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2012\par 15:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 In light of the current debate about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the peso versus the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governing council member Sebastian Claro said the bank doesn't have a determined peso level at which to launch such a program at the moment, newspaper La Tercera reported Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The peso has firmed some 10% against the dollar so far this year, the biggest gain for any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world in 2012.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a year-long \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program in 2011 when the peso appreciated to the CLP465 level versus the dollar in January of that year.\par \par \uc2 At the moment, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "doesn't have a level" to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Mr. Claro said in a Sunday interview.\par \par \uc2 The peso's strength is in part due to increased domestic spending and higher international copper prices, he said, noting that the peso is still trading in line with its fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Chile produces one third of the world's copper and the industrial metal accounts for 60% of the country's exports and 15% of gross domestic product. Copper prices have held relatively high, at over $3.50 a pound, for over a year.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the peso traded at around CLP470 to the dollar, prompting some sectors, such as agricultural producers, to intensify calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The problems of these sectors aren't solved with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Claro said.\par \par \uc2 In recent trading Monday, the peso was fetching CLP473.45 to the dollar versus Friday's close of CLP475.50, according to Valor Futuro newswire.\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 01-10-12 1353GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121001e8a1000s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
