\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Chile central bank \highlight\uc2  may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market, if needed\b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2012\par 16:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Peso weakens 0.51 pct vs U.S. dollar after comments\par \par \uc2  * Nominal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation common in emerging markets \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, details, context)\par \par \uc2  By Felipe Iturrieta\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Sept 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the peso's\par \par \uc2 strength if such a move is justified, bank president Rodrigo Vergara said on Friday.\par \par \uc2  "In exceptional periods, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Vergara told business leaders during an event in Santiago. " What is an exceptional period? An exchange rate that is significantly out of line with regard to its fundamentals for a relatively long period, because transitory things have less importance." \par \par \uc2  The peso dropped 0.51 percent to trade at 473.40 per U.S. dollar following Vergara's comments, and closed 0.76 percent weaker at 474.60 per dollar on Friday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has firmed nearly 10 percent this year on the back of prices for top export copper and firm local economic data.\par \par \uc2  The nominal appreciation of the Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a phenomenon common to all emerging markets, Vergara said. \par \par \uc2  South American officials, concerned that stronger domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will price their exports uncompetitively in the global market and drag on growth, have in the past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used a dollar-purchasing program last year to damp down the peso after it appreciated to its highest in more than 2-1/2 years at 465.50 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments weakened the peso because they leave the door open for a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The market isn't just speculating about the possibility of dollar purchases, but also bank deposit requirements," said Rodrigo Sarria, a trader at Celfin Capital in Santiago.\par \par \uc2  Tightening bank deposit requirements could slow the pace of credit expansion and curb domestic demand without having to hike interest rates, thus avoiding a further influx of capital that could boost the peso. \par \par \uc2  The peso's real exchange rate, which is an index the bank uses to show how competitive the peso is against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is at the low end of values coherent with its long-term fundamentals, Vergara said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained its key rate at 5 percent since a surprise cut in January, as it weighs solid domestic growth against external woes. \par \par \uc2  The world No.1 copper producer's small, export-dependent economy has so far resisted euro zone debt woes and slowing Chinese demand better than previously expected. \par \par \uc2  Vergara said one of the risks for the local economy was brisk domestic consumption, which adds inflationary pressure in the medium term.\par \par \uc2 "The reduction of internal risks for the economy happens via a necessary moderation of domestic demand," Vergara said.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month raised its forecast for domestic demand, which has been a pillar of Chile's economy, to 5.6 percent growth this year, from a previous forecast of 5.2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila, writing by Anthony Esposito; Editing by Bernadette Baum)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-CBANK/PESO (UPDATE 2) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121001e89s000ws\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
