\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Weaker, Reverses Early Gains After Spain Budget\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2012\par 18:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso closed slightly weaker against the dollar, reversing an early-session surge Thursday after Spain released its 2013 budget plan.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at CLP470.80 to the dollar, versus Wednesday's close of CLP470.50, after trading in a range of CLP468.00 to CLP472.49.\par \par \uc2 The peso crossed the psychologically important CLP470 level and traded at a one-year high early in the session on China's massive liquidity injection, but gave up its gains after Spain revealed it will tap 3 billion euros ($3.86 billion) from a reserve fund to cover its liquidity needs.\par \par \uc2 The peso often takes cues from European developments as the euro zone is one of Chile's main trading partners.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rodrigo Vergara reiterated an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has its costs.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vergara's comments "dispel the possibility of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sergio Tricio, head of research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chilean exporters, such as agricultural producers, have asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the peso.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a year-long \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program when the peso firmed to the CLP465 level in early January.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed \uc2 Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher mixed while the market awaits August industrial output and other economic data to be released early Friday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs closed at 2.32%, unchanged from Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.34%, from 2.37% on the previous session. Bond yields and prices move inversely.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 (Carolina Pica contributed to this article.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 27-09-12 1640GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120927e89r000yt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
