\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Governor Reiterates  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Has Costs\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2012\par 16:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 While the Chilean peso trades at a one-year high against the dollar and exporters clamor for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Rodrigo Vergara, the governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2 , reiterated Thursday that such a move has its costs.\par \par \uc2 In 2011, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market through daily purchases of $50 million for a total of $12 billion--which increased the bank's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to 15% of the country's gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 In a speech posted on the bank's website, Mr. Vergara said no measures such as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and capital controls are "cost free."\par \par \uc2 "A sterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worsens the balance sheet of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the interest rate on foreign reserves is lower than the interest rate on domestic debt," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  can increase international reserves during periods where access to international financing is tighter and they can also reduce misalignments, according to the central banker.\par \par \uc2 "Nonetheless, as it is not simple to define when there is a clear misalignment, there is always the risk of acting too soon, in which case the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be ineffective," Mr. Vergara said in prepared remarks delivered at the International Journal of Central Banking's fourth annual conference.\par \par \uc2 Regarding the quantitative easing measures central banks in developed economies adopted, Mr. Vergara said while these in principle should be good news for emerging markets as they aim to boost growth, they could have negative effects such as the "significant appreciation of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Write to Carolina Pica at carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 27-09-12 1526GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120927e89r000w1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
