\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Must Be 'Careful' if It  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -Ex Chief\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez  \par \uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2012\par 19:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 SANTIAGO, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --Despite some desperate calls for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't take up such a measure without carefully assessing its implications on the economy, former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Vittorio Corbo said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Although the Chilean peso has appreciated 10% versus the dollar so far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained hands-off while some of its peers in the region are taking steps to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The agricultural-export community, one of the victims of a strong peso, recently asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to be very careful with market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mr. Corbo on the sidelines of a seminar organized by financial-advisory firm Picton Advisors.\par \par \uc2 A distortion in the peso's parity against the dollar or the need to accumulate reserves are the two reasons for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; otherwise, an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be useless, Mr. Corbo added.\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a free-float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already increased its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to 15% of gross domestic product with its 2011 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't rule out a peso \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the cost of such a move would be too high, the current governor, Rodrigo Vergara, recently said.\par \par \uc2 On top of a strong peso, rising energy costs are also hurting agricultural exporters. Chile has some of the highest power-generation costs in the region as the Andean country imports thermal sources such as natural gas, coal and diesel, which represent a combined 62% of the country's installed capacity.\par \par \uc2 Chile's energy costs are a hurdle for the country's competitiveness and threaten its economic growth, Mr. Corbo said.\par \par \uc2 Energy costs could continue to rise after the Supreme Court recently halted the $5 billion, 2,100-megawatt Hacienda Castilla power project. The country needs to double its current 15,000-megawatt installed capacity over the next decade to keep up with projected demand and the cancellation puts this increase at risk.\par \par \uc2 "Energy costs are a problem" and Chile needs to reduce them to maintain growth, said Mr. Corbo.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently revised its GDP growth estimation upwards to between 4.75% and 5.25% this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires }}}\uc2  [ 26-09-12 1732GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120926e89q000wb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shp