\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Strengthens 1% After U.S. Fed Stimulus Move\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2012\par 13:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso strengthened 1% to a fresh 12-month high against the dollar Friday, a day after the U.S. Federal Reserve announced a new, open-ended round of quantitative easing to stimulate the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The peso crossed the significant CLP470 level and was trading recently at CLP467.70 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP472.50.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Fed announced a bond-buying program after its monetary policy meeting. Through this program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will pour more money into the U.S. market in an effort to stimulate the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 Local traders estimate some of this money will come to markets with higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as Chile's peso.\par \par \uc2 The Fed also said it would keep U.S. short-term interest rates near zero until 2015; it had said before it would keep rates low until late-2014.\par \par \uc2 In Chile, meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left the benchmark overnight rate, known locally as the TPM, unchanged at 5.0% for the eighth consecutive month Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's stimulus move also contributed to an increase in copper prices. As Chile produces one third of the world's copper, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  often moves in line with the industrial metal's price.\par \par \uc2 If the peso further appreciates against the greenback, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as it did during 2011 when the peso firmed to a 32-month high at CLP465.40 to the dollar in the first days of January.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean market has been active in early trading despite an upcoming long weekend to celebrate the country's Independence, a trader said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will close earlier Friday and trading will resume after the three-day Independence holiday Sept. 20.\par \par \uc2 (Peso quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 14-09-12 1215GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120914e89e000pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
