\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Strong  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso a worry but no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  now-cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2012\par 15:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Conditions for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  not met-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso has gained around 9 percent this year\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year to beat back peso\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and analyst quote, peso movements, copper)\par \par \uc2 By Felipe Iturrieta\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Rodrigo Vergara said on Friday that existing "worry" over the strong Chilean peso did not yet warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The peso has strengthened around 9 percent versus the U.S. dollar since the start of the year, sparking market speculation over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb peso strength, which exporters complain dulls their competitive edge globally.\par \par \uc2 "Naturally, there is worry over the topic of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Vergara told reporters when asked about the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 "Conditions for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not met. Nevertheless it's something we have to evaluate from moment to moment. It's not something we can exclude."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deployed a dollar-purchasing program last year, which lasted through December, to curb peso strength after it appreciated to its highest level in more than 2-1/2 years at 465.50 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso was trading around 0.36 percent stronger at 474.20 per dollar on Friday morning, buoyed as prices for Chile's top export copper rose to their highest in nearly four months.\par \par \uc2 "The simple fact of not showing so much worry over the peso gives it room to strengthen a little more," said Sergio Tricio, head of research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 He said a weaker global dollar and firmer copper prices\par \par \uc2 could push the peso to strengthen further and even break the 470 per dollar level.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila; Writing by Alexandra Ulmer Editing by W Simon)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-CBANK/EXCHANGERATE (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | C | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120907e897000s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
