\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher, Back at 4200 Level; Peso Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Graciela Ibanez   \par \uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2012\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 After Wednesday's local holiday, Chile's IPSA select-stock index ended higher Thursday tracking gains in U.S. shares after German Chancellor \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2  said she is committed to maintaining the euro.\par \par \uc2 The IPSA closed a preliminary 0.7% higher at 4212.23, while market volume declined to 71.70 billion Chilean pesos ($148.5 million) from CLP78.63 billion Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 As several of the heaviest-weighted shares on the IPSA are also listed in the U.S., the Chilean select index often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average.\par \par \uc2 The IPSA has been moving in the 4100 level in August as concerns about the euro zone's economy had continued to weigh on emerging markets. In July, the IPSA traded at the 4200-4400 area.\par \par \uc2 During Thursday's session, pulp and paper producer CMPC (CMPC.SN) released second-quarter earnings and reported a 76% decline year-on-year in net profit to $38.6 million on lower international pulp prices and the peso's appreciation versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Despite weaker earnings, CMPC ended 0.4% higher at CLP1,840.00.\par \par \uc2 Other gainers included retail holding company \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN), which ended 1.1% higher at CLP2,838.00. \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  has yet to release second-quarter results this month.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso closed weaker against the dollar as \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may give details of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP482.80 against the dollar, versus Tuesday's close of CLP482.40, after trading in a range of CLP482.00 to CLP484.75.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to hold the interest rate at 5% for the seventh straight month in its monthly monetary policy meeting Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In the fixed-income market, yields on inflation-indexed \uc2 Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed amid low inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCUs closed at 2.31%, unchanged from Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.43%, down from 2.45% in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Bond yields and prices move inversely to one another.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Graciela Ibanez at graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com [ 16-08-12 2016GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120816e88g000zg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
