\par\par \b \uc2 TAKE-A-LOOK Chile rate seen held in April, hiked later\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2012\par 14:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds latest stories) Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen holding its benchmark interest rate at 5.0 percent at its April 17 policy meeting, but then hiking the rate to 5.5 percent within 11 months, the bank's latest monthly poll of analysts showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The bank cut rates for the first time in 2-1/2 years in January on fears that key demand in Europe and top trading partner China would turn sluggish and hit the export-dependent country.\par \par \uc2 But a string of better-than-expected jobs, economic activity and manufacturing data coupled with an uptick in domestic inflation have flipped market bets from forecasting more cuts to betting on a hike by year-end.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par > Chile analysts see rate held in April, hiked later                 \par > Chile March exports down, imports up vs year ago                   \par > Chile rate seen held at 5 pct in April, coming mths                \par > Chile rates seen on hold as March inflation slows                  \par > Chile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raises 2012 GDP, CPI forecasts                  \par > Chile cenbank says only weighed rate hold in March                 \par > Chile Dec-Feb jobless rate eases sharply to 6.4 pct                \par > Chile cen bank president says rate neutral, no bias                \par > Chile cenbank holds key rate at 5.0 pct                            \par > TEXT-Chile cenbank holds key rate as expected                      \par > FACTBOX-Rate moves by Latin American central banks                 \par > \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cenbank has no trigger for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX inte