\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Head: No Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Planned\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2012\par 16:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market despite peso strength\par \par \uc2 --Letting the peso float freely allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to absorb shocks and react quickly\par \par \uc2 --Despite costs, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can never rule out market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , governor says\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from Vergara, background, in the fifth through ninth paragraphs.)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Chile (Dow Jones)--Despite the Chilean peso trading 7% stronger against the dollar since the year began, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have any plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the peso market, bank Governor Rodrigo Vergara said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In early 2011, when the peso was trading at three-year highs against the dollar, the bank launched a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 "[Market] \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only for extraordinary situations and it's not in our plans for now," he told reporters at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 However, he noted that a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can never rule out such a move if needed, but that the costs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are very high.\par \par \uc2 Vergara said the peso's exchange rate, when expressed in real terms, is in line with its long-term fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 When the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011, it said the peso's real exchange rate had deviated from its fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 During a presentation to the Icare local business forum, Vergara said a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as Chile's peso, is preferable to a pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it absorbs both internal and external shocks.\par \par \uc2 "It also allows for quicker [economic] adjustments when conditions rapidly change," Vergara said.\par \par \uc2 In the 1980s and 1990s, the Chilean peso was first fixed to the dollar and then moved in a narrow trading band, set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In 1999, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float freely.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 04-05-12 1049ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120405e845000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
